SUPPLY AGREEMENT v3
Harbour & Vale Retail Group and Orient Weave Garments Ltd (Hong Kong)
Apparel supply agreement - draft for legal review

Estimated annual supply value: £1,840,000

1. TERM AND TERMINATION
- Initial term: 3 years
- Automatic renewal for successive 3-year periods unless notice is given 12 months before expiry
- Termination for convenience: not permitted for the buyer during the initial term

2. PAYMENT TERMS
- Net 30 days from invoice
- Late payment interest: 8% a year above base rate

3. PRICE AND VOLUME
- Prices fixed for year 1; thereafter increased each year by CPI plus 2% with no cap
- Minimum purchase commitment: 80% of forecast volume, take-or-pay
- Exclusivity: the buyer may not source the same styles from any other supplier

4. DELIVERY AND PERFORMANCE
- Delivery: Ex-works Hong Kong
- On-time performance target: 90%, no service credits
- Quality AQL: 2.5%

5. LIABILITY AND LIMITATION
- Supplier liability capped at £250,000 in aggregate, excluding death or personal injury
- Excludes consequential and indirect damages including recall costs
- Buyer liability for unpaid invoices is uncapped

6. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
- Supplier retains ownership of patterns and tooling paid for by the buyer

7. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTES
- Hong Kong law; arbitration in Hong Kong

8. FORCE MAJEURE
- Standard force majeure with 30-day notice; includes supplier labour shortages and raw material price rises

DEVIATIONS FROM OUR STANDARD TERMS
Our standard terms: Net 60 payment, 1-year term with 90-day notice, liability cap of 100% of annual supply value,
fixed prices for the term, no exclusivity, buyer owns paid-for tooling, English law.
